J Ind Med</source><year>1993</year><volume>23</volume><fpage>301</fpage><lpage>12</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8427258</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Scherr</surname><given-names>PA</given-names></name><name><surname>Hutchison</surname><given-names>GB</given-names></name><name><surname>Neiman</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Non-Hodgkin's lymphoma and occupational exposure</article-title><source>Cancer Research</source><year>1992</year><volume>52</volume><fpage>5503</fpage><lpage>9</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mester</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Nieters</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Deeg</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Elsner</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Becker</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Seidler</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Occupation and malignant lymphoma: a population-based case-control study in Germany</article-title><source>Occup Environ Med</source><year>2006</year><volume>63</volume><fpage>17</fpage><lpage>26</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16361401</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1136/oem.2005.020453</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Harris</surname><given-names>NL</given-names></name><name><surname>Jaffe</surname><given-names>ES</given-names></name><name><surname>Stein</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Banks</surname><given-names>PM</given-names></name><name><surname>Chan</surname><given-names>JK</given-names></name><name><surname>Cleary</surname><given-names>ML</given-names></name><name><surname>Delsol</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>De Wolf-Peeters</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Falini</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Gatter</surname><given-names>KC</given-names></name><name><surname>Grogan</surname><given-names>TM</given-names></name><name><surname>Isaacson</surname><given-names>PG</given-names></name><name><surname>Knowles</surname><given-names>DM</given-names></name><name><surname>Mason</surname><given-names>DY</given-names></name><name><surname>M&#x000fc;ller-Hermelink</surname><given-names>H-K</given-names></name><name><surname>Pileri</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Piris</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Ralfkiaer</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Warnke</surname><given-names>RA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A revised European-American classification of lymphoid Non-Hodgkin lymphoma: a proposal from the International Lymphoma Study Group</article-title><source>Blood</source><year>1994</year><volume>84</volume><fpage>1361</fpage><lpage>92</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8068936</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jaffe</surname><given-names>ES</given-names></name><name><surname>Harris</surname><given-names>NL</given-names></name><name><surname>Stein</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Vardiman</surname><given-names>JW</given-names></name></person-group><source>Pathology and genetics of tumours of haematopoietic and lymphoid tissues. International Agency for Research on Cancer</source><year>2001</year><publisher-name>Lyon: IARC Press</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Becker</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Deeg</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Nieters</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Population-based study of lymphoma in Germany: rationale, study design and first results</article-title><source>Leukemia Research</source><year>2004</year><volume>28</volume><fpage>713</fpage><lpage>24</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15158093</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.leukres.2003.11.010</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Becker</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Deeg</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>R&#x000fc;diger</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Nieters</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Medical history and risk for lymphoma: results of a population-based case-control study in Germany</article-title><source>European Journal of Cancer</source><year>2005</year><volume>41</volume><fpage>133</fpage><lpage>42</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15617998</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.ejca.2004.08.028</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bolm-Audorff</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name><name><surname>Ahrens</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>J&#x000f6;ckel</surname><given-names>K-H</given-names></name><name><surname>Greiser</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Molik</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Timm</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Wichmann</surname><given-names>HE</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Hemon D, Goldberg M</surname></name></person-group><article-title>Experience with supplementary questionnaires in a lung cancer case reference study</article-title><source>Proceeding